# ("@/..."), or kept relative to the case's working directory ("rel:..."). What is recorded, in order: the transcript (every question, every line shown through `print_func`,
# everything printed to stdout), the return code or the exact refusal, every call to a launcher name the command reads
# (each wrapped there as a recording pass-through; `terminal_select` attribute by attribute), and every file left in the
# tree with its content. The real writer, payload, markdown and validators run, inside the tree; nothing else is touched.
